(1. Differential Maxwell Equations in Free Space) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.18 rg
(In vacuum without charges or conduction currents, the electromagnetic field obeys:) Tj T*
(1. Gauss's Law for Electricity: div\(E\) = 0) Tj T*
(2. Gauss's Law for Magnetism: div\(B\) = 0) Tj T*
(3. Faraday's Law of Induction: curl\(E\) = - d\(B\)/dt) Tj T*
(4. Ampere-Maxwell Law: curl\(B\) = mu_0 * eps_0 * d\(E\)/dt) Tj T*
T*
/F2 12.5 Tf
0.08 0.22 0.4 rg
(2. Displacement Current) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.18 rg
(James Clerk Maxwell identified that Ampere's original circuit law violated charge) Tj T*
(conservation for non-steady currents \(e.g. charging capacitors\). Adding the displacement) Tj T*
(current term mu_0 * eps_0 * d\(E\)/dt restored continuity and predicted wave propagation.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 12.5 Tf
0.08 0.22 0.4 rg
(3. Derivation of the Electromagnetic Wave Equation) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.18 rg
(Taking the curl of Faraday's Law and utilizing the vector identity curl\(curl\(E\)\) =) Tj T*
(grad\(div\(E\)\) - del^2\(E\) uncouples the fields into the wave equation:) Tj T*
(del^2\(E\) - mu_0 * eps_0 * d^2\(E\)/dt^2 = 0.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 12.5 Tf
0.08 0.22 0.4 rg
(4. The Speed of Light) Tj T*
/F1 10.5 Tf
0.15 0.15 0.18 rg
(The wave speed c = 1 / sqrt\(mu_0 * eps_0\) matches the measured speed of light,) Tj T*
(demonstrating that light is an electromagnetic disturbance.) Tj T*
